    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a bridge between abstract thinking and real-world problem-solving for me. While I enjoy its precision, it’s also intimidating due to its complexity—like trying to navigate a dense forest blindfolded. My parents didn’t emphasize it much, so I learned through trial and error, which made some concepts feel overwhelming at times.",
